WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.670 --> 00:47.672
[lively music]

00:51.384 --> 00:54.095
[indistinct chatter]

00:54.179 --> 00:55.972
[woman] Look at the leaves falling down.

00:56.931 --> 00:58.266
So pretty.

00:58.349 --> 00:59.851
[woman laughing]

01:00.435 --> 01:01.770
- You look so good.
- [camera clicks]

01:05.023 --> 01:07.859
- [girl] Hey, wait for me!
- [boy] Catch up already.

01:07.942 --> 01:08.943
[bell rings]

01:10.070 --> 01:12.322
[Ha-kyung] Seoul's current temperature
is at 21 degrees.

01:12.405 --> 01:16.159
Relative humidity, 43 percent.

01:17.243 --> 01:20.830
The North Pacific air mass
has moved on from Korea,

01:21.706 --> 01:26.628
taking the heat and humidity away,
and leaving perfect autumn weather.

01:29.631 --> 01:32.550
The migratory anticyclone
comes from the west this time of year,

01:32.634 --> 01:34.260
bringing this weather.

01:34.928 --> 01:36.346
When it's like this,

01:36.429 --> 01:39.265
there are a million things
to do outside, but I…

01:52.654 --> 01:54.948
can't do any with a broken heart.

01:55.031 --> 01:57.033
[light music]

02:07.293 --> 02:11.381
["Something Precious" by Rothy playing]

03:47.227 --> 03:51.439
[pensive music]

04:05.245 --> 04:06.871
I never even gave her a real present.

04:06.955 --> 04:09.123
[phone buzzing]

04:09.207 --> 04:10.458
[sighs]

04:12.543 --> 04:15.421
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

04:18.758 --> 04:20.176
[buzzing continues]

04:29.477 --> 04:30.436
Hey?

04:31.020 --> 04:32.105
It's Ha-kyung.

04:33.231 --> 04:35.942
The lotion you left,
should I throw it away?

04:36.025 --> 04:39.028
Uh, no, I'd still use it.

04:40.113 --> 04:41.864
Okay. I'll save it.

04:46.911 --> 04:48.204
The chargers

04:48.288 --> 04:51.624
that are plugged in at the window,
they're all yours?

04:51.708 --> 04:54.877
Oh, no, there's one that belongs
to Mr. Um, the black one.

04:59.924 --> 05:01.884
There's more than one black one.

05:02.468 --> 05:04.679
I'll pack them all.
And you two can figure it out.

05:05.263 --> 05:06.222
Okay.

05:07.974 --> 05:12.770
Hey, if you're gathering all my stuff,
you can leave it for now.

05:13.771 --> 05:14.772
I'll come later--

05:14.856 --> 05:18.109
It's fine. It's almost done.
I'll bring everything to Headquarters.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.069
I can come, it's heavy.

05:20.737 --> 05:22.613
- I'll stop by and--
- You don't have to.

05:22.697 --> 05:23.698
That's all.

05:26.743 --> 05:27.660
[beeps]

05:27.744 --> 05:29.746
[pensive music]

05:40.256 --> 05:41.382
[Ha-kyung sighs]

05:44.927 --> 05:46.929
[pensive music]

06:12.038 --> 06:17.085
EPISODE 14
MIGRATORY ANTICYCLONE

06:19.504 --> 06:21.506
[upbeat music]

06:50.785 --> 06:53.621
Director! Director!

06:53.704 --> 06:55.540
[water running]

06:56.332 --> 06:57.166
[sighs]

07:03.297 --> 07:07.093
Are you here for your stuff?
I told you I'd bring it to you. Hang on.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.928
Hey, something's wrong.

07:09.595 --> 07:10.555
What?

07:10.638 --> 07:12.807
They found out. About the two of us.

07:13.933 --> 07:14.934
Wh-what?

07:15.017 --> 07:16.644
That we were together.

07:17.770 --> 07:18.813
Huh?

07:18.896 --> 07:21.524
[playful music]

07:22.942 --> 07:25.445
Well, I heard
that you're dating Director Jin.

07:26.904 --> 07:27.822
What?

07:27.905 --> 07:29.866
So, when did it start?
While we were there?

07:30.992 --> 07:33.786
Wait. No, uh… Who did you hear that from?

07:33.870 --> 07:35.455
Nobody, really.

07:35.538 --> 07:37.790
Everyone on the team knew, I was the last.

07:38.708 --> 07:40.418
Everyone, how?

07:40.501 --> 07:41.711
I don't know.

07:42.670 --> 07:44.297
[Si-woo] That I was dating you.

07:45.006 --> 07:47.216
The whole team knows about what went on.

07:47.300 --> 07:49.260
You're seriously saying that…

07:49.343 --> 07:51.512
You're really sure everyone knows
that we dated?

07:51.596 --> 07:55.391
Yeah, I do. And by now,
the rumor's spread to all of the KMA.

07:55.475 --> 07:56.767
- What?
- [door opens]

07:57.351 --> 07:58.394
Uh, Mom!

08:03.858 --> 08:06.486
I just knew. I knew.

08:06.569 --> 08:08.029
How long have you been here?

08:08.112 --> 08:10.948
So you two had
a little office romance, didn't you?

08:11.032 --> 08:13.784
- Oh, Mom, no--
- Oh, I really just knew

08:13.868 --> 08:15.161
something was going on.

08:17.872 --> 08:20.249
- No way. We're not--
- Not what, huh?

08:21.167 --> 08:23.211
I also knew that you would deny it.

08:23.294 --> 08:25.963
So I brought my undeniable proof.

08:27.507 --> 08:30.134
[comical music]

08:32.178 --> 08:35.389
Take a good look. Still deny it?

08:35.473 --> 08:37.683
[quirky music]

08:37.767 --> 08:39.352
[nervous chuckle]

08:51.489 --> 08:53.491
[crickets chirping]

09:06.420 --> 09:09.882
[phone buzzing]

09:09.966 --> 09:13.386
FATHER

09:17.848 --> 09:18.849
[sighs]

09:22.103 --> 09:23.980
So, what's his family do?

09:24.939 --> 09:26.065
It doesn't matter.

09:28.234 --> 09:30.194
A mother has the right
to know things like that.

09:31.153 --> 09:32.697
Mom, it's of no concern to you.

09:32.780 --> 09:33.906
Why is that?

09:33.990 --> 09:35.283
[inhales sharply]

09:35.366 --> 09:37.451
'Cause it's old news. We called it off.

09:37.535 --> 09:38.661
Why?

09:38.744 --> 09:40.371
"If Mom thinks we broke up,
she won't snoop

09:40.454 --> 09:42.748
- and she'll leave us alone"?
- Ugh, oh, Mom!

09:42.832 --> 09:43.874
Is he Level Eight or Nine?

09:43.958 --> 09:45.918
Ugh, come on!

09:46.002 --> 09:48.170
You have to look at it for what it is.

09:49.380 --> 09:53.009
He's already off to a bad start
since he's got to be below you.

09:53.092 --> 09:54.802
He's younger, so it's all right.

09:54.885 --> 09:57.346
We won't count that,
and hope he makes up for it.

09:58.139 --> 09:59.390
- College?
- [Ha-kyung sighs]

09:59.473 --> 10:01.058
Parents are alive? Do you know?

10:01.142 --> 10:02.810
Where does he live?
And where did he grow up?

10:02.893 --> 10:04.270
I told you it's over.

10:04.854 --> 10:06.230
I have to know

10:06.314 --> 10:08.399
just what kind of family
he was raised with.

10:08.482 --> 10:10.401
- [Ha-kyung sighs]
- So I don't say the wrong thing.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.236
How can I make a good impression on them?

10:12.320 --> 10:14.572
I don't wanna say something rude.

10:14.655 --> 10:16.699
I told you, Mother, we broke up!

10:16.782 --> 10:18.576
You talk like I'm so great,

10:18.659 --> 10:22.413
and I went into it thinking I was, too,
but he dumped me. Do you get it?

10:22.496 --> 10:24.457
There's no way.
That's absolutely impossible.

10:25.291 --> 10:27.752
Find out his birthday, the date and time.

10:27.835 --> 10:28.669
Ugh, Mother!

10:30.046 --> 10:32.590
What? I wanna know if you're compatible.

10:32.673 --> 10:34.634
Ugh! Stop it!

10:36.510 --> 10:38.429
Ugh, now I have a headache.

10:38.929 --> 10:43.225
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

10:43.309 --> 10:45.728
[pensive music]

11:11.087 --> 11:12.338
[Si-woo] How's it going?

11:16.967 --> 11:19.095
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:21.847 --> 11:24.475
How's your mom? Did you fill her in?

11:24.558 --> 11:25.476
FATHER

11:25.559 --> 11:29.313
- [phone buzzing]
- [sighs]

11:30.314 --> 11:31.690
[line ringing]

11:31.774 --> 11:32.608
[exhales sharply]

11:32.691 --> 11:35.111
[operator] The person you are calling
is currently unavailable…

11:35.194 --> 11:37.863
[groans]
He never answers his phone.

11:37.947 --> 11:39.198
Can you tell us what happened?

11:39.281 --> 11:42.910
I was driving in the lane closest
to the sidewalk.

11:42.993 --> 11:44.120
I wasn't going fast at all.

11:44.203 --> 11:46.705
And then, that guy just jumped out
into the road.

11:46.789 --> 11:49.458
[man 1] There wasn't any way
for me to swerve or anything.

11:49.542 --> 11:52.044
- Oh, we got another fucking idiot.
- [man 1] I didn't do anything wrong.

11:53.003 --> 11:55.339
You're really saying
you did nothing wrong?

11:55.423 --> 11:57.716
You hit me 'cause you were speeding.

11:57.800 --> 12:00.010
Maybe I was wrong for crossing the street.

12:00.094 --> 12:01.720
You did nothing wrong,
and I look like this?

12:02.430 --> 12:04.014
- I--
- How did you do nothing wrong!

12:04.098 --> 12:06.684
[groaning]

12:07.643 --> 12:10.521
Ah, shit.
[huffs]

12:12.648 --> 12:14.024
[exhales sharply]

12:14.108 --> 12:16.110
[somber music]

12:23.033 --> 12:24.076
Okay.

12:29.206 --> 12:31.792
Oh, I made breakfast. We can eat together.

12:32.376 --> 12:34.378
I'm not that hungry this morning.

12:34.462 --> 12:36.338
Uh, Yu-jin,
I made the dumpling soup you like.

12:36.422 --> 12:38.048
Look. It's good.

12:39.133 --> 12:41.385
Uh… Sorry.

12:41.469 --> 12:43.679
I'm not feeling great. I can't today.

12:44.472 --> 12:45.431
Ah.

12:51.520 --> 12:52.521
[sighs]

12:59.945 --> 13:00.988
[Ki-jun] Yu-jin.

13:01.947 --> 13:03.032
Yeah?

13:04.408 --> 13:05.451
I wanted to let you know,

13:05.534 --> 13:09.830
we can register things later,
if you want to.

13:11.707 --> 13:13.751
Time's not a big deal.

13:13.834 --> 13:16.128
I'd rather do it
when we can both be excited together.

13:24.970 --> 13:27.723
Neither of us have been
in a relationship this serious.

13:27.806 --> 13:29.016
Marriage and all.

13:29.099 --> 13:33.062
There's so many dumb things
that I've done, and you had to deal with.

13:33.145 --> 13:35.147
And I realized it, and I'm ashamed.

13:35.731 --> 13:38.609
I thought if I tried to be tough
and keep it in, then…

13:39.193 --> 13:40.528
it would be better for you.

13:42.071 --> 13:44.782
And I now know that I just made things
harder for you.

13:47.785 --> 13:48.786
Anyway…

13:50.246 --> 13:52.289
I'm gonna work very hard
to get better, Yu-jin.

13:52.957 --> 13:56.460
[pensive music]

13:58.921 --> 14:00.297
I want this to work.

14:01.173 --> 14:02.341
Hm?

14:02.925 --> 14:04.552
Oppa.

14:11.350 --> 14:13.352
You shouldn't go all morning
with an empty stomach.

14:13.435 --> 14:15.020
Could I get you some milk?

14:15.854 --> 14:16.939
Mm-hm.

14:17.022 --> 14:19.275
Good. Okay, get dressed now.

14:26.657 --> 14:29.243
[pensive music]

14:45.259 --> 14:46.343
[sighs]

15:18.751 --> 15:20.753
[lively music]

15:35.935 --> 15:37.895
- [door closes]
- [lock beeping]

15:42.274 --> 15:43.609
[exhales sharply]

15:44.234 --> 15:46.946
[bright music]

15:51.075 --> 15:53.827
[mewls, giggles]

15:58.832 --> 16:00.000
[lock beeps]

16:03.921 --> 16:04.922
[sighs]

16:06.173 --> 16:08.175
[automated voice] Twelfth floor.

16:08.258 --> 16:09.635
- Doors opening.
- Oh.

16:10.386 --> 16:12.680
[upbeat music]

16:12.763 --> 16:13.931
It's you.

16:14.014 --> 16:16.016
[nervous chuckle]
Ha-kyung.

16:20.396 --> 16:22.439
Uh, I'm, um… I'm here to, uh, go…

16:23.190 --> 16:24.984
- Because I--
- Our mom sent you?

16:25.067 --> 16:25.901
Huh?

16:26.819 --> 16:27.820
[grumbles]

16:30.114 --> 16:31.699
[automated voice] Doors closing.

16:32.783 --> 16:34.201
Doors opening.

16:34.785 --> 16:36.996
Come on, you're being too harsh.

16:37.079 --> 16:39.665
Our Mother only does this
'cause she cares.

16:39.748 --> 16:40.958
How can you defend her?

16:41.041 --> 16:43.419
There's no excuse
for her sending you this early!

16:43.502 --> 16:46.672
Sorry, I thought if I came early,
we'd have time to talk.

16:46.755 --> 16:48.799
We didn't realize you left so early.

16:48.882 --> 16:50.551
Why is she so obsessed?

16:50.634 --> 16:52.720
Why does it matter
if I get married or not?

16:53.220 --> 16:55.597
I said we broke up,
why doesn't she believe me?

16:55.681 --> 16:57.391
You what? Who's the guy?

16:58.559 --> 16:59.560
Go home.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.146
Our mom needs to stay away.
Can you tell her that for me?

17:02.229 --> 17:03.480
Actually, I'll call her.

17:03.564 --> 17:05.607
No, don't! You can't.

17:05.691 --> 17:07.192
Ma would kill me.

17:07.276 --> 17:09.862
What are you talking about?
And what did you do to her?

17:09.945 --> 17:10.821
Huh?

17:12.031 --> 17:15.367
Hey, I know how you are when you're mad.
You're gonna blow up at her.

17:15.451 --> 17:18.579
You say all this awful stuff,
and then run away.

17:18.662 --> 17:21.123
And she goes on for days.
I can't run away.

17:21.206 --> 17:23.625
She mopes around,
and comes up with a million plans.

17:23.709 --> 17:25.627
"This is the one!" Ugh!

17:25.711 --> 17:27.296
No, Jin Ha-kyung.

17:27.379 --> 17:30.674
I'm begging, take an hour to cool off
before you call her.

17:30.758 --> 17:33.844
It seems like a really bad idea
to make this call right now.

17:33.927 --> 17:34.970
I can't allow it.

17:35.054 --> 17:36.764
For my sake, you can't call her.

17:38.098 --> 17:40.142
[upbeat music]

17:40.225 --> 17:41.518
Fine. All right.

17:42.436 --> 17:43.771
[sighs]

17:43.854 --> 17:45.314
Sometimes you're great.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.653
I owe you one, or something.

17:51.737 --> 17:52.988
[scoffs]

17:53.072 --> 17:55.282
You didn't see me today. Get to work.

17:56.950 --> 17:58.368
I'll go first. Okay. See ya.

18:02.873 --> 18:03.832
[sighs]

18:09.755 --> 18:10.798
Sweetheart.

18:12.132 --> 18:13.592
Take a look at this.

18:13.675 --> 18:14.760
[chuckles]

18:15.803 --> 18:16.887
What is it?

18:19.098 --> 18:20.808
Well, it's…

18:23.602 --> 18:24.978
- [squeaks]
- [automated voice] Dear Bo-mi.

18:25.062 --> 18:26.063
Happy birthday!

18:26.146 --> 18:28.357
[chuckles]
It's funny.

18:29.983 --> 18:32.319
Right? It doubles as an alarm, too.

18:32.402 --> 18:35.864
It can attach to her backpack.
You think she'll like it? Do you?

18:37.491 --> 18:38.909
Bo-mi is in seventh grade.

18:38.992 --> 18:40.702
I know. Are you messing with me?

18:40.786 --> 18:43.413
No, for her age,
the bear is not a great present.

18:44.665 --> 18:45.916
[clinks]

18:45.999 --> 18:48.001
Really? They said it's the new thing.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.419
Ugh!

18:50.003 --> 18:51.630
I'm going to school.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.132
Not before you eat.

18:53.799 --> 18:55.425
My stomach's upset.

18:56.218 --> 18:57.302
Her stomach's upset?

18:57.386 --> 18:58.595
It's monthly.

18:59.680 --> 19:00.597
What?

19:00.681 --> 19:02.432
- Bo-mi, at least drink this.
- [lock chimes]

19:03.350 --> 19:04.393
It's monthly.

19:06.937 --> 19:08.730
- [door closes]
- [lock chimes]

19:08.814 --> 19:10.482
Oh, it's her…

19:16.071 --> 19:18.323
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

19:18.407 --> 19:20.242
[man] Hey, did you hear
that they're dating?

19:20.325 --> 19:21.994
- [woman] Really?
- [man] Yeah.

19:22.077 --> 19:23.745
[woman 2] Really? They're dating?

19:23.829 --> 19:25.664
[employees chatter indistinctly]

19:25.747 --> 19:27.666
[woman 3 whispers]
I heard it's Director Jin from Team Two.

19:28.417 --> 19:30.836
I HEARD THEY'RE DATING

19:30.919 --> 19:32.254
ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:33.255 --> 19:34.756
HOW LONG HAS IT BEEN?

19:34.840 --> 19:36.300
REALLY?
I HEARD HE'S WITH DIRECTOR JIN

19:36.383 --> 19:38.719
THEY LOOK GOOD TOGETHER

19:38.802 --> 19:39.887
[sighs]

19:39.970 --> 19:43.056
THEY'RE GOING OUT

19:43.140 --> 19:44.558
THEY ARE?
THEY'RE REALLY DATING?

19:44.641 --> 19:46.351
REALLY? ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:48.770 --> 19:50.814
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

19:58.572 --> 20:00.574
[indistinct chatter]

20:04.203 --> 20:05.579
[man 1] I heard they're dating.

20:05.662 --> 20:06.914
[woman 1] How long?

20:06.997 --> 20:08.248
[woman 2] Look.

20:10.459 --> 20:11.793
[man 2] Do you know if it's true?

20:12.794 --> 20:15.505
Forecaster Lee Si-woo
and Director Jin Ha-kyung?

20:15.589 --> 20:17.049
They're really dating?

20:17.132 --> 20:18.508
[employees whispering]

20:19.092 --> 20:20.761
[man 3] You think
she'll get married this time?

20:20.844 --> 20:23.138
- [man 4] They're great together.
- They're both good-looking.

20:23.222 --> 20:25.265
[birds twittering]

20:25.349 --> 20:26.642
[sighs]

20:30.979 --> 20:33.607
[indistinct chatter]

20:34.775 --> 20:35.859
[groans]

20:41.323 --> 20:42.282
[sighs]

20:43.575 --> 20:45.369
[Myung-ju humming]

20:48.038 --> 20:50.040
I really hope you thought this through.

20:50.749 --> 20:52.167
I guess you might as well.

20:52.834 --> 20:53.794
What?

20:55.254 --> 20:57.422
Director Ha-kyung isn't just a co-worker.

20:58.340 --> 21:01.385
We all saw what happened
her first time dating a co-worker.

21:01.468 --> 21:02.844
It was awful for her.

21:03.929 --> 21:06.306
You wouldn't call things off
just 'cause of the speculation,

21:06.390 --> 21:07.474
you like her a lot.

21:07.557 --> 21:10.352
They say, "Heavy is the head
that wears the crown." Right?

21:11.186 --> 21:13.730
- That's how it goes.
- I guess so.

21:15.607 --> 21:18.110
But, uh, Mrs. Oh, actually, we--

21:18.193 --> 21:21.196
You'll be fine. I'm rooting for you two.

21:22.572 --> 21:24.783
I hope everything works out.

21:25.492 --> 21:28.287
And of course, that Director Jin
won't get hurt again.

21:28.370 --> 21:30.289
It's good that she's
with someone like you.

21:31.373 --> 21:34.126
If she was headed for a Ki-jun repeat,
there's a chance that

21:34.209 --> 21:38.213
she could actually end up in Geneva,
so she can really start over.

21:39.298 --> 21:41.842
Oh, and between the two of us, uh, we…

21:41.925 --> 21:45.470
Well, Team Two cannot handle
another new director.

21:46.179 --> 21:47.389
Not this year.

21:48.348 --> 21:51.268
We're finally sort of beginning
to work well.

21:52.019 --> 21:53.020
Yeah.

21:54.146 --> 21:57.149
I'm sure that you both knew
going into things

21:57.232 --> 21:58.692
that it was worth all the risk.

21:59.651 --> 22:03.822
If it was just a fling or anything,
that wasn't serious, then, well…

22:04.448 --> 22:06.908
- we never would've known.
- [both chuckle]

22:06.992 --> 22:08.618
- Yeah.
- Mm.

22:10.078 --> 22:12.164
Don't let all the talk get to you.

22:13.707 --> 22:14.750
Okay?

22:14.833 --> 22:17.252
- Good luck, Si-woo.
- Okay. Thank you.

22:25.135 --> 22:26.136
[sighs]

22:29.931 --> 22:31.433
[exhales heavily]

22:40.025 --> 22:44.571
[phone buzzing]

22:46.114 --> 22:47.365
What do you need?

22:49.409 --> 22:50.494
What do we do?

22:50.577 --> 22:54.247
Everyone thinks that we're really serious
about each other.

22:54.331 --> 22:55.499
[Ha-kyung] Ignore it.

22:55.582 --> 22:58.001
Don't listen and don't comment.
Just ignore it.

22:58.085 --> 22:59.336
And then they'll move on.

22:59.419 --> 23:01.213
There will be a lot
of new gossip soon enough.

23:02.380 --> 23:05.175
- Yeah, or we could--
- If this isn't about work, I'm hanging up.

23:05.258 --> 23:07.886
You can't call me at work
to talk about this stuff.

23:07.969 --> 23:09.346
[elevator dings]

23:14.518 --> 23:17.104
[somber music]

23:31.576 --> 23:32.869
[indistinct chatter]

23:32.953 --> 23:34.955
- Good work.
- [man] Thank you, sir.

23:44.881 --> 23:46.591
- Great work, sir.
- Mm.

23:47.342 --> 23:48.802
What should we look out for?

23:49.594 --> 23:51.096
Yeah, well, there's not much today.

23:53.849 --> 23:56.393
[Ha-kyung] The upper-level trough
around the Baikal

23:56.476 --> 23:58.937
seems to be developing unusually quickly.

23:59.020 --> 24:01.106
It will still be within a week or so.

24:01.189 --> 24:03.024
[Young-gil] Some days
the weather's just great.

24:03.775 --> 24:06.444
And we got through the busy season,
which helps.

24:06.528 --> 24:08.655
You should go on a date with this weather.

24:11.658 --> 24:13.785
Well, there are many other things to do
in good weather.

24:14.369 --> 24:16.913
If things are slow
with live monitoring for today,

24:16.997 --> 24:20.375
you could look into the first frost dates
for the last 30 years.

24:20.458 --> 24:22.252
Get a head start for winter?

24:22.335 --> 24:24.546
You want to start right now?

24:25.422 --> 24:26.506
[Young-gil] Oh, come on.

24:26.590 --> 24:29.050
We just cleared busy season.
Can't we breathe a little?

24:29.134 --> 24:32.012
Just 'cause it's over,
doesn't mean we can get complacent.

24:33.513 --> 24:36.141
There's always a cyclone
after a migratory anticyclone.

24:36.224 --> 24:37.976
The smallest change in the air current

24:38.059 --> 24:40.478
can lead to disaster,
so we've got to stay on our toes.

24:40.562 --> 24:43.690
Also, please keep things professional
when we're working.

24:43.773 --> 24:45.108
[chuckles]

24:45.192 --> 24:46.860
Of course, I will. I will.

24:47.444 --> 24:49.112
It was just a joke, though.

24:50.113 --> 24:52.157
You don't need to make
a big deal out of it.

24:58.914 --> 24:59.789
[soft chuckle]

25:03.752 --> 25:06.463
[somber music]

25:19.768 --> 25:22.187
[creaking]

25:23.813 --> 25:25.815
[quirky music]

25:36.952 --> 25:38.119
[Mrs. Bae] Oh, boy.

25:44.376 --> 25:46.211
You just got here or are you leaving?

25:46.294 --> 25:47.462
Uh…

25:48.296 --> 25:49.673
You remember Mi-seon, don't you?

25:49.756 --> 25:51.091
We went to middle school together.

25:51.174 --> 25:53.510
Yesterday, there was a party
for her newest book,

25:53.593 --> 25:56.012
and I had a drink or a few.
[nervous chuckle]

25:56.096 --> 25:57.555
She wrote another one?

25:57.639 --> 25:58.932
Oh.

25:59.015 --> 26:00.809
What are you gonna do?

26:01.393 --> 26:05.105
She's younger, published more.
Meanwhile, you've done what?

26:05.188 --> 26:07.274
So when are you gonna get a party?

26:08.024 --> 26:09.317
Well, really soon.

26:09.401 --> 26:11.444
I'm just working everything out right now.

26:11.528 --> 26:15.073
You don't ever know
if it'll happen till it's done.

26:15.156 --> 26:18.034
When are you going to get a real job?
This is too unreliable.

26:18.118 --> 26:20.245
- One more year? How long?
- [scoffs]

26:20.328 --> 26:21.329
Oh, Mom.

26:21.413 --> 26:23.290
I can write a bestseller. You don't know.

26:23.373 --> 26:26.126
Get the book finished
and show me the numbers.

26:26.209 --> 26:27.669
And then we can talk.

26:27.752 --> 26:28.628
Okay?

26:29.337 --> 26:32.007
Good grief.
I've got two perfectly capable kids.

26:32.090 --> 26:35.218
Why won't they let me help them
to be happy?

26:35.302 --> 26:38.096
Mom, just leave Ha-kyung alone,
would you?

26:38.179 --> 26:41.474
Who cares who she's dating
or if she ever gets married?

26:41.558 --> 26:43.268
She lied to you about it, too?

26:43.351 --> 26:44.352
What?

26:44.436 --> 26:46.771
Ha-kyung's dating
the Team Two guy. I know.

26:46.855 --> 26:48.064
Team who?

26:48.148 --> 26:50.775
She's dating a co-worker? Who is it?

26:51.401 --> 26:52.610
It's that guy, you know.

26:52.694 --> 26:55.613
The tall one. He could be on TV.

26:55.697 --> 26:57.532
Pale face, he could be an actor.

26:58.241 --> 27:01.828
The only guy I know who…
Is it Shin Seok-ho?

27:01.911 --> 27:03.413
Shin Seok-ho now?

27:03.496 --> 27:05.707
The guy above Ha-kyung.
They're on the same…

27:05.790 --> 27:08.084
- They both work on Team Two.
- [mumbles]

27:08.877 --> 27:10.920
That guy is not tall at all.

27:11.004 --> 27:13.048
He's pale, but he's not that handsome.

27:13.131 --> 27:15.800
I think he could definitely be an actor.

27:17.677 --> 27:21.139
Well, anyway, Mother, who…
Who is she going with?

27:21.222 --> 27:22.807
Lee Si-woo is the guy.

27:24.017 --> 27:27.645
You know him. It's the guy
she had to go to Jeju with.

27:28.229 --> 27:30.982
I know for a fact
they've been seeing each other.

27:31.066 --> 27:33.693
And they think they can lie
to my face about it?

27:33.777 --> 27:35.195
Why wouldn't they lie?

27:35.278 --> 27:37.280
Mother, you know how you are
with these things.

27:37.364 --> 27:38.573
What'd I do?

27:38.656 --> 27:41.284
"What's his family like?
What does his father do?"

27:41.368 --> 27:44.079
"What college? What's his level at work?"

27:44.162 --> 27:46.539
"What day was he born? What hour?"

27:46.623 --> 27:49.959
Ha-kyung told you that?
That I asked her about that stuff.

27:50.043 --> 27:52.670
[scoffs]
No, Ha-kyung doesn't have to say a thing.

27:52.754 --> 27:54.756
You asked that about every guy
we've mentioned.

27:54.839 --> 27:56.925
It wasn't all of them.

27:57.425 --> 28:00.804
Mother, you have to let it go.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.555
You only mess things up

28:02.639 --> 28:04.766
when you insert yourself
and manage her life.

28:05.725 --> 28:08.269
It's a big deal that she's dating at all.

28:08.353 --> 28:10.438
You should be excited just for that, huh?

28:10.522 --> 28:14.067
- I get it. Enough. I'll stop.
- Uh-huh?

28:14.150 --> 28:15.318
I just care!

28:17.904 --> 28:19.656
- Hang on.
- Hm?

28:19.739 --> 28:21.074
Where did you sleep last night?

28:21.157 --> 28:22.534
Oh, Shin Se…

28:24.661 --> 28:25.703
Shin's guest bed.

28:25.787 --> 28:27.163
Wasn't it Mi-seon's party?

28:27.747 --> 28:30.959
Uh, Shin came to the party, too.
There were lots of people there.

28:32.293 --> 28:34.129
You don't need to know any of that!

28:36.714 --> 28:39.717
[quirky music]

28:40.301 --> 28:41.177
[door closes]

28:43.012 --> 28:44.180
[exhales sharply]

28:46.141 --> 28:47.100
[sighs]

28:48.184 --> 28:50.478
It's terrifying that she can always tell.

28:53.523 --> 28:55.275
- [phone vibrates]
- Hmm?

28:59.028 --> 29:00.739
[Seok-ho] Why did you sneak out
this morning?

29:00.822 --> 29:02.365
I was going to make you coffee.

29:06.494 --> 29:08.079
[phone vibrates]

29:11.249 --> 29:13.752
[Tae-kyung] What are your plans
this evening?

29:13.835 --> 29:15.003
[chuckles]

29:18.757 --> 29:19.966
[giggles, clears throat]

29:20.633 --> 29:22.010
[Seok-ho] I'm totally free.

29:23.511 --> 29:25.263
- [Myung-ju] Mr. Um.
- Yeah?

29:25.346 --> 29:28.016
I've got the regional temperature analysis
you wanted.

29:28.099 --> 29:29.726
- I'll take a look.
- Okay.

29:29.809 --> 29:31.978
Oh, also, how old are your boys right now?

29:32.061 --> 29:34.522
The eldest is ten,
and the youngest is now eight.

29:34.606 --> 29:37.400
- Why?
- You probably wouldn't know, then.

29:37.484 --> 29:38.902
Huh? Know what?

29:39.611 --> 29:43.948
- Oh, I… Well, it's Bo-mi's birthday soon.
- Oh.

29:44.032 --> 29:47.702
And I have no idea
what kids that age are into.

29:47.786 --> 29:50.955
Ah, Bo-mi's in middle school.
So, what grade is she in?

29:51.039 --> 29:51.873
Seventh.

29:52.540 --> 29:53.750
Seventh.

29:53.833 --> 29:54.876
Brand-name things.

29:55.627 --> 29:57.253
Brand names?
[chuckles]

29:57.337 --> 29:59.130
What are you talking about? She's a kid.

29:59.214 --> 30:00.965
Hm? Haven't you heard?

30:01.049 --> 30:04.385
Your teenagers all love brand names,
you know? It's the new thing.

30:04.969 --> 30:07.388
My niece said she wanted a Valen coat

30:07.472 --> 30:10.308
from her mom if she scored well
in the next PSAT coming up.

30:10.391 --> 30:11.601
- [Myung-ju scoffs]
- For real?

30:13.812 --> 30:15.730
Tell me, aren't those real expensive?

30:15.814 --> 30:17.398
It's designer. Of course, it is.

30:17.482 --> 30:18.983
- Yeah, right?
- [Myung-ju] Mm.

30:20.944 --> 30:22.278
[Dong-han] What the…

30:22.362 --> 30:23.446
[both gasp]

30:24.113 --> 30:25.865
They get this stuff for kids?

30:25.949 --> 30:28.660
[Myung-ju] Wow, this is crazy expensive.
[gasps]

30:28.743 --> 30:31.204
I haven't even looked at a coat
that costs so much money.

30:31.287 --> 30:33.748
- Just for a coat?
- [approaching footsteps]

30:33.832 --> 30:34.958
[Ha-kyung] Soo-jin.

30:35.041 --> 30:37.710
Could you look at the data
for the migratory cyclone movement

30:37.794 --> 30:40.088
for September to October
from the last decade?

30:40.171 --> 30:42.590
Huh? The whole decade?

30:43.174 --> 30:44.384
Yes. The whole thing, please.

30:47.095 --> 30:48.054
Okay.

30:50.890 --> 30:52.851
Wow, what do I…

30:52.934 --> 30:54.727
You don't have to spend
that kind of money.

30:55.228 --> 30:56.938
There are plenty
of other things she'll love.

30:57.522 --> 30:59.315
How does anyone afford a coat like that?

31:00.149 --> 31:02.902
- Jeez.
- Do they wear it to school?

31:04.362 --> 31:05.905
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

31:08.658 --> 31:10.368
[Sung-jin]
Well, have you thought about it?

31:13.663 --> 31:15.665
Ms. Im took a leave of absence?

31:15.748 --> 31:17.417
- Mm-hm.
- Why?

31:17.500 --> 31:19.419
Her husband was transferred
to the US branch,

31:19.502 --> 31:21.963
- so she's moving out there for a bit.
- Mm…

31:22.046 --> 31:24.132
So, we'll need someone to fill in.

31:24.716 --> 31:25.592
Right.

31:26.885 --> 31:30.513
I was thinking, you said you wanted
to transfer over to Policy, right?

31:30.597 --> 31:33.391
I do. You don't know
how many times I've applied.

31:33.975 --> 31:35.977
I think you should give it another shot.

31:36.060 --> 31:38.980
The director, right now,
I think he'd take you in a second.

31:39.063 --> 31:40.940
- Seriously?
- Mm-hmm.

31:46.237 --> 31:48.573
SOO-JIN, HAVE YOU MADE UP YOUR MIND?

31:49.282 --> 31:50.325
[sighs]

31:55.538 --> 31:58.666
Who's currently working
on the 24-hour forecast?

32:00.752 --> 32:01.836
I am.

32:04.047 --> 32:06.883
[quirky music]

32:07.634 --> 32:09.218
How long till we can send it out?

32:09.302 --> 32:12.305
Hmm, it'll be done in an hour, I'd say.

32:15.850 --> 32:18.895
I also need that cyclone development data
from Baikal Lake.

32:19.479 --> 32:21.064
I'll have them for you soon as well.

32:22.732 --> 32:25.985
I'm putting it on a chart.
That way, it'll be easier to look at.

32:30.740 --> 32:32.241
No, that's okay. Just the data.

32:32.825 --> 32:35.411
- It's not hard to do.
- Just the data.

32:35.495 --> 32:36.621
Okay.

32:44.212 --> 32:46.130
[murmurs] Ignore him. Focus.

32:53.012 --> 32:55.974
Mr. Kim, would you go
to the Model Department right now

32:56.057 --> 32:58.101
and get me the data
on the three-month outlook?

32:58.184 --> 32:59.686
[chuckling]

33:02.105 --> 33:02.981
[Ki-jun] Mr. Kim.

33:03.564 --> 33:06.234
That kid is so distracted.
He never pays attention.

33:08.569 --> 33:11.864
[chuckling]

33:11.948 --> 33:15.994
[Eun-joo] When did Director Jin Ha-kyung
and Forecaster Lee Si-woo start dating?

33:16.077 --> 33:18.287
[Jung-hwan] You know what they say,
misery loves company.

33:18.371 --> 33:21.457
That reporter Chae Yu-jin used to date
Lee Si-woo before she got married.

33:21.541 --> 33:23.251
[Young-sin]
Wait. So that's not a love triangle.

33:23.334 --> 33:25.586
- [Eun-joo] A love square?
- [Jae-yoon] It's something, for sure.

33:25.670 --> 33:26.546
[Ki-jun] Too much free time?

33:27.213 --> 33:29.298
[gasps]
Sir.

33:30.800 --> 33:32.385
Oh, I'm sorry, sir.

33:33.136 --> 33:35.430
I don't say anything. Ever.

33:39.767 --> 33:41.185
Go to the Model Department,

33:41.269 --> 33:42.937
see what they have
for the next three months

33:43.021 --> 33:44.480
and bring it back here, please.

33:44.564 --> 33:45.481
Yep.

33:51.821 --> 33:52.822
[door opens]

33:56.367 --> 33:59.162
[Eun-joo] Do you think Mr. Han
and Ms. Chae know?

33:59.245 --> 34:00.913
[Jung-hwan] Everyone's heard by now.

34:00.997 --> 34:03.666
That's why you shouldn't date co-workers.

34:07.462 --> 34:08.671
[sighs]

34:26.105 --> 34:27.940
[keyboard clacking]

34:36.741 --> 34:38.993
[pensive music]

34:56.344 --> 34:58.596
The climate outlook report
for this winter…

34:59.347 --> 35:02.266
I think you'll need to add more
on the possibility of a La Niña.

35:02.350 --> 35:03.559
LA NIÑA: A PHENOMENON IN THE EQUATORIAL
REGION OF THE EASTERN PACIFIC OCEAN

35:03.643 --> 35:05.978
Okay. Is it because of the NOAA?

35:06.062 --> 35:07.438
It's not just them.

35:08.189 --> 35:10.858
The ECWMF, the Australian,
and the Japanese forecasts

35:10.942 --> 35:12.860
have La Niña predictions this winter.

35:13.611 --> 35:15.905
Whatever we're saying,
I need it by four o'clock.

35:16.405 --> 35:18.366
If you can get it in any earlier,
that'd be great.

35:32.839 --> 35:34.006
Is there something else?

35:37.051 --> 35:39.178
It looks like
there's something you want to say.

35:43.057 --> 35:44.809
[breathes deeply]

35:45.434 --> 35:49.814
I've known Ha-kyung for over ten years,
that's a while.

35:49.897 --> 35:52.316
In that time, I got too used to her.

35:52.984 --> 35:55.403
It was too easy to forget
how amazing she is.

35:55.486 --> 35:57.113
I came to take her for granted.

35:58.489 --> 36:00.700
I completely lost perspective on her.

36:00.783 --> 36:04.287
When I should've realized what we had
and been thankful,

36:04.370 --> 36:06.581
I got further from reality
and more resentful.

36:07.331 --> 36:09.083
What are you telling me exactly?

36:12.795 --> 36:15.506
I was really the asshole
in our story together.

36:18.092 --> 36:20.178
And it's different from the two of you.

36:20.261 --> 36:22.597
Ha-kyung will have trouble
moving on from you.

36:23.097 --> 36:27.351
[somber music]

36:28.686 --> 36:30.438
Well, uh, she broke it off.

36:30.521 --> 36:32.398
You think that will get you off the hook?

36:34.650 --> 36:38.154
Nobody really cares if you're together
or if you're not, you know that?

36:39.280 --> 36:43.159
What they wanna know
is the reason why it happened.

36:46.412 --> 36:50.416
When you date in the office,
or have any kind of drama,

36:51.083 --> 36:55.796
somehow, women always end up
getting hit harder than the men do.

36:55.880 --> 37:00.551
So Ha-kyung didn't just get hurt by me,
the office was judging her as well.

37:00.635 --> 37:01.844
But…

37:02.970 --> 37:05.223
you've had a taste of how that is, too.

37:05.932 --> 37:09.518
She really shouldn't have to deal
with all that gossip any longer.

37:10.102 --> 37:12.480
- I know that.
- So then…

37:13.981 --> 37:15.024
[exhales sharply]

37:15.524 --> 37:18.027
I'm the last person
who should be saying this.

37:19.403 --> 37:21.864
Fight the break up
unless you're totally sure.

37:24.200 --> 37:27.995
If you're sure that things are ending,
do what you can to help her.

37:30.206 --> 37:32.166
Do the opposite of what I did.

37:36.963 --> 37:39.966
[somber music]

37:40.049 --> 37:41.133
[sighs]

37:43.719 --> 37:46.430
[Ha-kyung] The cold weather could hit
the south sooner than we thought.

37:46.514 --> 37:48.683
We'll ask
the Forecast Analysis team first.

37:48.766 --> 37:51.852
And then, if it's confirmed,
we'll tell Impact Forecast right away.

37:52.395 --> 37:53.354
All right.

37:54.939 --> 37:57.650
What are you saying?
That it's gonna be cold?

37:58.192 --> 38:01.696
In Siberia, the anticyclone
is developing faster than expected,

38:01.779 --> 38:03.656
so the temperature will drop.

38:03.739 --> 38:06.784
Look here, the core of the cold wave,
it's headed in that direction.

38:06.867 --> 38:10.246
So the North Atlantic anticyclone
has migrated away to the east,

38:10.329 --> 38:13.666
and that cold continental anticyclone
from the lake is speeding up.

38:14.542 --> 38:16.335
In those positions, it will get cold.

38:16.419 --> 38:17.753
What about near Daegwallyeong?

38:17.837 --> 38:21.299
It looks like the temperature
will go below zero inland by tomorrow,

38:21.382 --> 38:23.467
around Daegwallyeong and Cheorwon.

38:23.551 --> 38:25.845
Mr. Shin, what was our forecast
for this week?

38:26.345 --> 38:29.098
We've predicted that the temperatures
in those particular areas

38:29.181 --> 38:30.683
will drop this weekend.

38:30.766 --> 38:33.352
If the temperature drops
by 10 degrees or more,

38:33.436 --> 38:35.313
the sudden change
will feel like a big shock.

38:35.396 --> 38:37.398
He's right. That's not good.

38:38.399 --> 38:39.317
[Team Manager 1 sighs]

38:40.109 --> 38:42.486
It'll impact the farmers
all over the country.

38:42.570 --> 38:43.654
They're about to harvest.

38:44.363 --> 38:47.283
It's almost kimchi season.
So the radishes on Ganghwa Island

38:47.366 --> 38:50.077
and the cabbage crop in Gangwon
could be severely damaged,

38:50.661 --> 38:54.040
plus the soybeans and chili peppers
from North Gyeongsang, too.

38:55.583 --> 38:58.544
We'll monitor for a little longer
and see if there's a clear pattern,

38:58.627 --> 39:00.588
and decide if we need a warning
and when to send it out.

39:00.671 --> 39:03.090
For the farmers, reach out
to the local governments,

39:03.174 --> 39:04.508
warn them to prepare for the cold.

39:04.592 --> 39:05.968
They'll do what they can.

39:06.052 --> 39:09.221
But if a cyclone was developing this fast
with those temperatures,

39:09.930 --> 39:12.600
I would've expected your team
to notify us sooner.

39:13.392 --> 39:16.937
I guess we all know how it is
with a new boyfriend, right?

39:20.691 --> 39:22.610
- [Dong-han] Hey, Mr. Kim.
- Huh?

39:22.693 --> 39:24.111
How's your wife these days?

39:24.695 --> 39:26.238
- Good.
- Great.

39:27.698 --> 39:30.743
Did you know Mrs. Kim
used to work at the KMA?

39:30.826 --> 39:31.911
[Dong-han chuckles]

39:31.994 --> 39:33.412
[Myung-ju] Hm, so she did.

39:33.496 --> 39:37.416
I remember you two
had a… whirlwind romance, didn't you?

39:37.500 --> 39:40.336
Oh, remember all the PDA?
And whenever you fought,

39:40.419 --> 39:42.505
the whole office held their breath?

39:42.588 --> 39:44.799
[Myung-ju] Yeah, everyone
was so scared of you two.

39:44.882 --> 39:47.218
- 'Cause if they broke up… Ugh!
- [Dong-han] What a huge deal.

39:47.301 --> 39:49.887
Well, anyway, I should head
to the Spokesperson's Office.

39:49.970 --> 39:51.847
We'll reach out
to those local governments.

39:51.931 --> 39:52.932
[clears throat]

39:53.849 --> 39:57.520
He's having a day. It's a mid-life crisis.

39:57.603 --> 39:58.896
I'll talk to him, okay?

40:02.024 --> 40:04.276
You didn't have to do that, Mr. Um.

40:04.360 --> 40:08.072
I did. Otherwise, people
would just keep disrespecting you.

40:10.032 --> 40:11.158
[Myung-ju] He's right.

40:11.242 --> 40:13.452
We're here to work, not to make jokes.

40:13.536 --> 40:16.330
He should know better
than to comment on your personal life.

40:16.414 --> 40:18.040
Please, he does know better.

40:18.999 --> 40:21.877
So, there's a cold wave coming in, right?

40:22.503 --> 40:23.796
Let's get to work.

40:23.879 --> 40:25.631
[Ha-kyung] I have something to say first.

40:28.592 --> 40:29.510
We have…

40:34.265 --> 40:36.142
Forecaster Lee Si-woo and I--

40:36.225 --> 40:38.436
Thank you for all your support.

40:38.519 --> 40:39.728
[Si-woo chuckles]

40:39.812 --> 40:42.690
We're just here to work. Keep it separate.

40:44.108 --> 40:45.317
Was that it?

40:48.362 --> 40:49.405
[Dong-han] Yeah.

40:49.488 --> 40:51.073
Okay.
[chuckles]

40:52.366 --> 40:54.160
No PDA, okay, you two?

40:54.785 --> 40:56.370
[all chuckling]

40:56.454 --> 40:58.164
- Ooh!
- [Si-woo chuckles]

41:00.374 --> 41:03.169
[pensive music]

41:15.931 --> 41:18.559
Why did you say that in there?
What was that?

41:19.143 --> 41:21.896
Let's keep it… a secret for a while.

41:21.979 --> 41:22.980
What?

41:23.063 --> 41:24.273
That we're not together.

41:24.356 --> 41:25.608
What are you saying?

41:27.193 --> 41:29.195
You know, it'll be so annoying,

41:29.278 --> 41:33.532
if people think we just started dating,
and then we break up right away.

41:33.616 --> 41:36.911
Everyone is going to speculate
about what went wrong so quickly.

41:36.994 --> 41:39.038
It's just asking for extra gossip.

41:39.622 --> 41:43.083
So I thought we should pretend
we're still dating for a while.

41:43.667 --> 41:44.960
So it won't be such a big deal.

41:45.711 --> 41:46.795
You're trying to spare me?

41:49.840 --> 41:52.718
You're trying to protect me
from everyone, from the gossip?

41:52.801 --> 41:53.719
That's the idea?

41:55.262 --> 41:56.263
It's not…

41:57.681 --> 42:00.601
Then it's because right now
you look like the villain?

42:00.684 --> 42:02.770
- It's not.
- There has to be something.

42:02.853 --> 42:04.355
I just don't want to hear it.

42:05.397 --> 42:08.526
I don't wanna hear people talking
about you like they really know.

42:08.609 --> 42:10.569
'Cause I can't handle anymore.

42:12.863 --> 42:13.989
That's why.

42:14.073 --> 42:16.784
[somber music]

42:16.867 --> 42:19.787
You didn't know? That's what happens
when you date in the office.

42:20.454 --> 42:22.831
Whether it ends in marriage
or incredible heartbreak,

42:22.915 --> 42:25.459
they all turn it into gossip
for the group chat.

42:27.670 --> 42:29.338
I knew that going in.

42:31.131 --> 42:33.592
Still, I chose to do it again.

42:33.676 --> 42:37.388
["Love Hurts a Little More"
by Kim Na Young]

42:41.183 --> 42:42.768
- I'm sorry.
- Don't say that to me.

42:43.394 --> 42:44.937
I knew the risks.

42:45.020 --> 42:47.982
I chose to start it. It's my own doing.

42:49.567 --> 42:51.110
So don't say you're sorry.

42:51.193 --> 42:55.072
What happens from here
isn't anything I haven't seen before.

42:55.656 --> 42:57.324
It's not for you, though.

43:00.744 --> 43:03.455
I struggle with everything.

43:06.166 --> 43:07.334
It's been awful.

43:09.837 --> 43:11.714
[Si-woo] I didn't want you to get hurt,

43:12.464 --> 43:14.300
just because I can't play clingy.

43:15.009 --> 43:15.884
I didn't know…

43:17.886 --> 43:21.265
doing that would hurt you even more.

43:30.065 --> 43:31.150
[sighs]

43:49.293 --> 43:50.419
Chae Yu-jin.

43:52.254 --> 43:54.214
The column is yours from now on.

43:55.007 --> 43:56.008
Hm?

43:56.967 --> 43:59.428
Isn't this the special article Se-hui
was working on?

44:00.387 --> 44:04.099
She's with child.
She needs to take it easy for a while.

44:04.683 --> 44:06.727
Wow. She's having a baby?

44:06.810 --> 44:08.479
[cackles]

44:09.271 --> 44:11.690
She thinks she's so special for it.

44:11.774 --> 44:14.151
And she didn't apologize for anything.

44:15.444 --> 44:17.363
Well, she's probably nervous about it all.

44:18.238 --> 44:20.908
I wish she'd take a leave of absence
till she has the thing.

44:21.492 --> 44:24.203
At least we could get a temporary
or something if she did that.

44:24.286 --> 44:26.622
It's inconsiderate,
and we're stuck with her.

44:27.456 --> 44:29.667
How long am I in charge of the column?

44:29.750 --> 44:31.210
It's yours now.

44:32.294 --> 44:33.212
What?

44:33.879 --> 44:36.548
It's on you. You've got it forever.

44:37.341 --> 44:42.096
Realistically, having a kid means
that she won't get back to work

44:42.179 --> 44:43.305
for a year or two.

44:43.806 --> 44:46.266
Women do that,
and they get out of practice.

44:46.350 --> 44:47.935
Article quality goes down.

44:48.018 --> 44:50.938
And if they can't catch up,
they get kicked to the curb, you know?

44:51.021 --> 44:53.148
[scoffs]
There's no way.

44:53.649 --> 44:56.026
I only mean that she'll get back, and…

44:56.110 --> 44:58.070
[laughs]

44:58.153 --> 44:59.988
What? You don't believe it?

45:00.906 --> 45:02.324
Ask anyone here.

45:02.408 --> 45:07.162
Do you know how many reporters
never come back after kids?

45:08.122 --> 45:11.834
This is a great opportunity for you,
so don't mess it up.

45:13.085 --> 45:15.337
You always said you wanted
your own column.

45:15.963 --> 45:19.299
This column is on the front page, my dear.

45:19.842 --> 45:21.093
That's a great spot.

45:23.429 --> 45:24.471
Yeah.

45:25.305 --> 45:26.348
Thank you, sir.

45:27.891 --> 45:29.685
Okay. Get to it.

45:35.607 --> 45:36.608
[sighs]

45:38.902 --> 45:41.905
[somber music]

45:46.952 --> 45:49.913
Penny for your thoughts?
You look so pretty.

45:49.997 --> 45:52.624
[chuckles]
Nothing.

45:54.209 --> 45:56.628
Really? What's going on?

45:58.172 --> 45:59.298
[sucks teeth]

45:59.381 --> 46:02.301
They gave the column to me,
so there's that.

46:02.384 --> 46:03.427
Seriously?

46:03.510 --> 46:05.929
Are you kidding?
Yu-jin, really, it's all yours?

46:06.013 --> 46:07.264
[Yu-jin sighs]

46:07.347 --> 46:09.725
Oh, why the face? That's fantastic.

46:10.267 --> 46:11.435
Oh…

46:11.518 --> 46:13.979
Oh, I have this briefing now,
and then I'm off.

46:14.521 --> 46:16.273
Let's go and grab a drink to celebrate.

46:16.940 --> 46:18.233
I can't have alcohol.

46:18.317 --> 46:21.111
Why? Still not feeling well?

46:24.114 --> 46:26.241
What is it, Yu-jin? Please tell me.

46:26.325 --> 46:27.409
I can handle it.

46:28.869 --> 46:30.579
What, you need a computer?

46:30.662 --> 46:32.831
Or a new purse? We can go to the mall.

46:34.625 --> 46:35.792
[Yu-jin] I'm…

46:36.376 --> 46:37.753
I'm pregnant.

46:45.302 --> 46:46.178
Huh?

46:47.179 --> 46:48.889
I'm 12 weeks along.

46:49.890 --> 46:53.769
[pensive music]

46:57.773 --> 47:01.360
Good job, everybody.
Let's call it a little early.

47:01.944 --> 47:04.112
- [man] Okay.
- Okay.

47:05.405 --> 47:07.407
[pensive music]

47:18.877 --> 47:19.836
[door closes]

47:43.068 --> 47:43.944
Hmm.

47:45.028 --> 47:46.655
[Myung-ju] Running late, Mr. Shin?

47:46.738 --> 47:48.365
Huh? Oh, uh…

47:49.408 --> 47:51.702
You're gaming, aren't you? Good luck.

47:51.785 --> 47:54.496
- No. Um…
- Where are you going, then?

47:55.205 --> 47:57.291
Is it a blind date? Is it?

47:58.667 --> 48:00.711
- It's not.
- What is it?

48:00.794 --> 48:02.754
- [automated voice] Doors opening.
- He said no?

48:07.259 --> 48:08.260
[Myung-ju] Hello.

48:10.387 --> 48:12.097
[alarm blaring]

48:12.180 --> 48:13.098
Huh.

48:14.558 --> 48:16.435
- You're the last one.
- [alarm continues blaring]

48:17.519 --> 48:18.562
No.

48:19.229 --> 48:21.898
I have a very important appointment today.

48:21.982 --> 48:23.066
Hey.

48:25.444 --> 48:26.445
I'll get off.

48:26.528 --> 48:27.613
[alarms stop blaring]

48:28.822 --> 48:30.365
- Okay.
- Excuse me.

48:32.409 --> 48:35.120
- [employees oohing]
- [indistinct murmurs]

48:35.203 --> 48:37.080
[employees chuckling]

48:43.128 --> 48:43.962
[exhales sharply]

48:45.631 --> 48:46.840
This is so weird.

48:47.633 --> 48:49.009
I didn't notice.

48:50.677 --> 48:54.514
How long are we gonna act
like we're still together?

48:54.598 --> 48:56.224
Just until…

48:56.892 --> 48:58.685
they stop talking about it.

49:05.442 --> 49:07.110
You really want us to lie?

49:07.194 --> 49:08.236
Yes.

49:09.029 --> 49:10.030
I prefer it for now.

49:19.331 --> 49:20.248
[Ha-kyung sighs]

49:20.832 --> 49:24.878
[phone buzzing]

49:24.961 --> 49:26.838
HAN KI-JUN

49:31.885 --> 49:34.971
[phone buzzing]

49:35.055 --> 49:36.848
CHAE YU-JIN

49:39.393 --> 49:42.688
[both phones buzzing]

49:50.278 --> 49:51.238
[man] Welcome.

49:55.283 --> 49:58.078
[gentle music]

50:28.108 --> 50:31.236
[panting]

50:33.155 --> 50:34.906
Huh? Hey!

50:36.450 --> 50:37.659
Oh!

50:40.412 --> 50:41.705
I thought the traffic was…

50:41.788 --> 50:45.625
Yeah, the traffic was awful,
so you took the subway.

50:45.709 --> 50:47.753
You got off too early, yeah?

50:48.628 --> 50:51.381
[both chuckling]

50:54.092 --> 50:55.844
So, do you wanna go eat?

51:02.476 --> 51:04.060
[both moaning]

51:07.606 --> 51:09.149
- Aah!
- Oh, god. God!

51:09.232 --> 51:11.526
- [Tae-kyung screams]
- Sorry, sorry, sorry. What did I do? Okay.

51:11.610 --> 51:14.196
- Ow! My hair.
- Oh, god. Wait, wait, wait. I'm sorry.

51:14.780 --> 51:17.324
- There. I got it. Are you okay?
- That hurt.

51:17.407 --> 51:19.159
[stutters]
I'm so sorry.

51:20.786 --> 51:22.120
[chuckles]

51:22.746 --> 51:24.873
[smooches, moans]

51:26.291 --> 51:27.459
Ow! Ow!

51:29.002 --> 51:30.712
[groaning]

51:30.796 --> 51:31.838
Oh! What happened?

51:31.922 --> 51:34.299
- [Seok-ho groans]
- It's okay. I'm so sorry.

51:34.925 --> 51:36.468
- [groans]
- What do I do?

51:37.886 --> 51:38.929
[both chuckle]

51:39.012 --> 51:40.639
[both moaning]

51:48.104 --> 51:48.939
[door slams]

51:51.024 --> 51:53.777
- [Ki-jun sighs]
- You must think I'm an idiot.

51:54.277 --> 51:55.946
Mm-hmm. You're an idiot.

51:56.029 --> 51:57.864
I just didn't know what to do,

51:58.657 --> 52:01.326
the right thing to say,
or how I should be reacting.

52:03.620 --> 52:05.997
I barely managed to say anything at all.

52:08.917 --> 52:12.170
[pensive music]

52:12.754 --> 52:14.965
[sighs]
Still, I don't know how he…

52:15.465 --> 52:17.843
I tell him I'm pregnant
and he says that to me.

52:18.426 --> 52:19.594
Oh, uh…

52:20.345 --> 52:23.682
I-I thought…
that we are waiting to do… that.

52:23.765 --> 52:26.393
[scoffs]
Why would he say that?

52:27.894 --> 52:29.354
What were you expecting?

52:30.355 --> 52:33.608
I mean, I don't know.
Something better than that.

52:34.109 --> 52:35.694
That he always wanted to be a dad.

52:35.777 --> 52:37.487
Or, "How are you feeling?"

52:37.571 --> 52:38.989
Something supportive.

52:41.324 --> 52:42.325
[sighs]

52:45.704 --> 52:47.789
What? Okay.

52:50.041 --> 52:52.919
You love him a lot, don't you?

52:54.588 --> 52:55.714
[Yu-jin sighs]

52:56.298 --> 52:57.799
I thought he'd be better since he's older.

52:57.883 --> 53:00.927
Instead, he's like a teenager,
ever since the wedding.

53:01.511 --> 53:02.762
He's so immature.

53:04.389 --> 53:07.058
I thought marriage would be easy
and he'd take care of me.

53:07.601 --> 53:08.852
But this is harder.

53:09.895 --> 53:11.855
It feels like he's getting
more and more distant.

53:13.106 --> 53:14.941
And we fight all the time.

53:18.278 --> 53:20.196
No relationship is easy.

53:20.780 --> 53:23.867
If we can't get along
with our own parents, then…

53:24.534 --> 53:26.620
It's never been easy with my dad.

53:28.455 --> 53:31.833
Parents, children,
married couples, siblings…

53:31.917 --> 53:33.835
Things only get tougher with time.

53:34.544 --> 53:35.712
And with family.

53:35.795 --> 53:37.672
You expect more from them,

53:38.924 --> 53:40.216
so you get upset.

53:43.762 --> 53:45.722
Feels like I made the right choice.

53:47.557 --> 53:49.142
I'll never go through this with a wife.

53:51.853 --> 53:52.771
Right?

53:53.855 --> 53:56.608
Why? Something happened with the Director?

54:00.445 --> 54:02.614
It's over. We're done.

54:07.953 --> 54:10.872
If she's 12 weeks along, there's plenty
of time before the baby comes

54:10.956 --> 54:12.540
to apologize and prepare.

54:13.124 --> 54:14.626
Yeah, what about the money?

54:15.418 --> 54:18.630
Even now, we're stretched thin
with rent and bills.

54:19.631 --> 54:21.967
All right, but don't think of telling her
you'll go halfsies.

54:22.050 --> 54:24.469
English preschools are so expensive.

54:24.552 --> 54:25.679
[chuckles]

54:25.762 --> 54:27.806
You're getting a few years
ahead of yourself.

54:27.889 --> 54:30.684
You have to start them
when they're young, or else…

54:30.767 --> 54:32.102
And I can't teach them.

54:37.649 --> 54:39.275
You are excited, though.

54:42.320 --> 54:44.531
I feel…
[sighs deeply]

54:46.032 --> 54:48.743
worried more than excited. What if I…

54:50.203 --> 54:51.496
I'm a bad dad.

54:52.455 --> 54:55.709
I barely even know
how to not be an awful husband.

54:55.792 --> 54:56.793
[sighs]

55:00.380 --> 55:01.673
You'll be a good dad.

55:05.510 --> 55:06.678
You're gonna be great.

55:08.304 --> 55:11.683
You always do the best you can
when you care about things.

55:12.267 --> 55:15.061
If only I wasn't such
a picky perfectionist.

55:15.145 --> 55:17.981
[somber music]

55:19.983 --> 55:22.652
So things with Lee Si-woo
went south, I heard.

55:29.701 --> 55:31.036
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung.

55:34.664 --> 55:37.250
One person wanting a relationship
isn't enough.

55:37.751 --> 55:40.211
What do you say is the reason?
That doesn't make sense.

55:41.755 --> 55:45.008
Oh, you know, he gave lots of reasons.
This and that.

55:45.091 --> 55:46.676
But it was that…

55:47.385 --> 55:48.803
I wasn't good enough.

55:48.887 --> 55:52.640
What… There's no way.
You're the coolest person I know.

55:53.224 --> 55:54.225
Huh?

55:54.309 --> 55:58.188
You're intelligent, good at your job,
responsible, really good at sports.

55:58.271 --> 56:01.066
If you don't know you're a ten,
I don't know how to help you.

56:02.817 --> 56:05.028
- You dumped me, too.
- Huh?

56:09.741 --> 56:11.326
Oh, that's just…
[sighs]

56:11.409 --> 56:13.328
It's fine. That's all over now.

56:15.455 --> 56:17.707
It's strange that it ended
like that twice.

56:18.291 --> 56:20.502
It's a sign that I'm bad at relationships.

56:21.086 --> 56:22.128
Hey.

56:23.254 --> 56:24.756
So tell your wife you're sorry.

56:24.839 --> 56:26.382
And don't drink anymore.

56:26.466 --> 56:29.135
Go get her flowers
or some other nice things from the store.

56:29.219 --> 56:31.387
Go now. Good night.

56:32.722 --> 56:34.307
It's 'cause I'm an idiot.

56:35.517 --> 56:37.560
You couldn't have been more wonderful.

56:39.979 --> 56:42.524
You're a real catch,
you know, Jin Ha-kyung?

56:42.607 --> 56:46.027
[emotional music]

56:48.113 --> 56:49.155
Good night.

57:06.422 --> 57:10.969
[phone buzzing]

57:12.428 --> 57:14.013
LEE SI-WOO'S FATHER

57:20.270 --> 57:21.396
Hello?

57:22.272 --> 57:23.731
[Si-woo] There wasn't a day

57:24.399 --> 57:27.235
I didn't wish my father was different.

57:27.902 --> 57:29.404
But there was nothing I can do.

57:30.155 --> 57:31.656
My mom and dad…

57:34.117 --> 57:35.660
acted like I…

57:36.244 --> 57:38.246
I did something wrong by being born.

57:39.622 --> 57:41.040
It was all my fault.

57:43.710 --> 57:45.670
It was my fault that my mom

57:47.005 --> 57:49.132
had to give up her work and stay home.

57:50.008 --> 57:52.469
My fault she got sick and passed away.

57:53.595 --> 57:56.890
He said she would've lived a long life
if I never came along.

57:59.726 --> 58:00.935
She only died,

58:02.145 --> 58:04.105
because I took so much out of her.

58:04.856 --> 58:06.107
That's terrible.

58:07.901 --> 58:10.236
If you can't handle that,
don't have a kid.

58:11.321 --> 58:12.572
It's awful

58:13.573 --> 58:16.409
when the people that brought you
into this world think

58:19.037 --> 58:20.622
you're what's wrong.

58:39.557 --> 58:40.642
Oh, honey.

58:41.309 --> 58:42.185
Sorry.

58:43.686 --> 58:44.646
[woman sighs]

58:44.729 --> 58:45.980
[woman] My mom's worse.

58:46.064 --> 58:48.608
More than we thought
she'd be at this point.

58:49.234 --> 58:51.861
Uh-huh. Se-chan and I are coming home.

58:53.571 --> 58:56.908
Oh, honey, the bus is here.
I'll call you back, okay?

59:03.414 --> 59:05.083
I'm sorry, just a second.

59:05.667 --> 59:06.751
[grunting]

59:06.834 --> 59:08.211
Here, I can get that.

59:08.294 --> 59:10.630
Oh, thank you. Thank you so much.

59:11.631 --> 59:14.968
[melancholic music]

59:15.051 --> 59:17.303
- Oh, get on.
- Okay. Thank you.

59:20.098 --> 59:22.100
[baby sobbing]

59:22.183 --> 59:25.353
Don't cry, Se-chan. Aw, it's okay.

59:25.436 --> 59:28.022
[baby crying]

59:30.525 --> 59:32.193
[woman] I'm sorry, she's tired.

59:33.027 --> 59:34.195
[baby wailing]

59:35.321 --> 59:36.948
Aw, it's okay.

59:39.242 --> 59:44.205
Realistically, having a kid means
that she won't get back to work

59:44.289 --> 59:45.373
for a year or two.

59:45.957 --> 59:48.501
Women do that,
and they get out of practice.

59:48.585 --> 59:50.044
Article quality goes down.

59:50.128 --> 59:53.423
And if they can't catch up, they're
getting kicked to the curb, you know?

59:54.507 --> 59:56.175
[baby wails]

59:56.968 --> 01:00:00.013
[pensive music]

01:00:08.688 --> 01:00:09.939
Welcome home.

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:13.234
You must be tired. I'll hang that up.

01:00:14.694 --> 01:00:15.737
Why?

01:00:21.159 --> 01:00:23.119
I haven't congratulated you yet.

01:00:23.620 --> 01:00:25.121
[Ki-jun] I'm sorry about before.

01:00:25.663 --> 01:00:27.624
I freaked out. I was an idiot.

01:00:28.708 --> 01:00:30.418
I was surprised, that's all.

01:00:34.922 --> 01:00:36.591
I'm sorry it's been so hard.

01:00:36.674 --> 01:00:38.259
Especially for you.

01:00:38.843 --> 01:00:40.386
I love you, Yu-jin.

01:00:50.605 --> 01:00:52.482
I have an appointment
with the doctor next week.

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:55.860
Y-You do?

01:00:56.444 --> 01:00:57.737
When? What day?

01:00:57.820 --> 01:00:59.906
I should be there, too. I'll come with.

01:01:01.324 --> 01:01:02.283
[inhales deeply]

01:01:03.034 --> 01:01:05.370
I was thinking
we shouldn't see it through.

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:08.539
I don't know
how we'd take care of the kid.

01:01:13.044 --> 01:01:14.545
What are you saying then?

01:01:15.588 --> 01:01:17.423
You know you don't want it either.

01:01:18.049 --> 01:01:21.302
You're so stressed about money. And this…
[inhales sharply]

01:01:22.303 --> 01:01:23.721
It's not a good idea.

01:01:24.430 --> 01:01:27.600
Yu-jin, are we gonna…

01:01:29.018 --> 01:01:30.311
We're not ready, oppa.

01:01:30.395 --> 01:01:31.479
Hm?

01:01:32.188 --> 01:01:35.483
[pensive music]

01:01:35.566 --> 01:01:36.859
[inhales sharply]

01:01:41.531 --> 01:01:43.533
[crickets chirping]

01:01:54.001 --> 01:01:56.003
[somber music]

01:02:10.101 --> 01:02:11.644
[Si-woo] There's no such thing…

01:02:13.187 --> 01:02:14.897
as guaranteed happiness.

01:02:16.149 --> 01:02:17.650
That's why I had to leave.

01:02:18.151 --> 01:02:19.861
I've tried so hard and I…

01:02:20.695 --> 01:02:23.322
I can't figure out
how to be happy in life.

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:26.075
And I couldn't…

01:02:27.618 --> 01:02:29.996
live with sharing any unhappiness
with her.

01:02:31.622 --> 01:02:32.707
That's why.

01:02:49.182 --> 01:02:50.975
Oh, uh, good evening, ma'am.

01:02:53.019 --> 01:02:55.354
This is so weird.
I happened to be in the neighborhood--

01:02:55.438 --> 01:02:56.939
Where's Ha-kyung right now?

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:58.107
What?

01:02:58.191 --> 01:03:00.276
Where's Ha-kyung? Was she with you?

01:03:09.076 --> 01:03:11.245
I'm looking for Lee Myung-han.

01:03:11.329 --> 01:03:12.789
Of course, one moment.

01:03:12.872 --> 01:03:15.541
Are you Mr. Lee's guardian?

01:03:18.002 --> 01:03:18.920
Uh, sort of.

01:03:20.004 --> 01:03:21.756
We brought him in from a car accident.

01:03:22.256 --> 01:03:25.134
And when we ran some of the basic tests,

01:03:25.218 --> 01:03:26.844
we found something that looks off.

01:03:27.595 --> 01:03:29.764
- Is it an issue?
- Uh, yeah.

01:03:31.474 --> 01:03:34.685
[phone buzzing]

01:03:34.769 --> 01:03:36.479
LEE SI-WOO

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:44.445
[line ringing]

01:03:44.529 --> 01:03:47.281
[sighs]
Answer your phone. Please, please.

01:03:51.369 --> 01:03:53.162
[redials, line rings]

01:03:54.622 --> 01:03:55.623
[slams]

01:03:55.706 --> 01:03:58.209
[somber music]

01:04:00.628 --> 01:04:02.171
[Mrs. Bae clears throat]

01:04:02.255 --> 01:04:03.172
Hey, you.

01:04:04.632 --> 01:04:06.050
Oh, yes?

01:04:06.133 --> 01:04:08.010
I've wanted to chat with you.

01:04:08.594 --> 01:04:10.221
Hm. Sure.

01:04:12.223 --> 01:04:14.934
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:16.435
LEE SI-WOO

01:04:16.519 --> 01:04:19.605
[Myung-han snoring]

01:04:24.485 --> 01:04:27.321
[reporter] The weather's been pleasant
the past few days.

01:04:27.405 --> 01:04:29.407
However, an unexpected cold snap

01:04:29.490 --> 01:04:31.742
coming in may cause
some trouble for farmers.

01:04:31.826 --> 01:04:33.953
Cold weather encourages staying in,

01:04:34.036 --> 01:04:36.956
withdrawing not just physically,
but mentally as well.

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:39.333
We recommend that everyone
at home take extra care

01:04:39.417 --> 01:04:41.752
to maintain their immune system
and their mental health.

01:04:44.672 --> 01:04:47.300
[snoring]

01:04:47.383 --> 01:04:49.385
["Abnormal Climate" by Giriboy playing]

01:05:31.010 --> 01:05:32.887
So then, when do we expect it to end?

01:05:32.970 --> 01:05:34.013
As things stand--

01:05:34.096 --> 01:05:36.349
The forecast will have
to be reversed possibly.

01:05:36.432 --> 01:05:38.476
You're going to take a bullet
for what Si-woo said?

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:39.518
Say that again!

01:05:39.602 --> 01:05:41.437
- Oh, uh…
- Hey, knock it off!

01:05:42.438 --> 01:05:44.106
[Ha-kyung] Did you already know?

01:05:44.190 --> 01:05:45.232
You need a biopsy.

01:05:45.316 --> 01:05:47.234
[Si-woo] My relationships
always started out great

01:05:47.318 --> 01:05:50.029
but my father would always ruin them.

01:05:50.112 --> 01:05:51.614
[Ha-kyung] Because you'll regret it.

01:05:51.697 --> 01:05:54.367
You might regret it later.

01:05:54.450 --> 01:05:56.160
I still like you a lot.

01:05:57.411 --> 01:05:58.371
[Si-woo] Do you know that?
